  "question": {
    "text": "Structures of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in solid state, vapour phase and at very high temperature respectively are:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Monomeric, Dimeric, Polymeric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Dimeric, Polymeric, Monomeric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Polymeric, Monomeric, Dimeric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Polymeric, Dimeric, Monomeric",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is dimeric in vapour phase. The coordination number of beryllium is 3.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0019_8f5b27075e80.png\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is monomeric at high temperature.&nbsp;The coordination number of beryllium is 2.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0019_09fa79622612.png\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 56px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is polymeric in solid state.&nbsp;The coordination number of beryllium is 4.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0019_1e2824452fc8.png\" /></p></blockquote>"
  }
}